  "notes": "The Shaytan and the angels are never drawn; his promise (48:6-15) is not glossed, and As-Sa'di's report of his appearance is not used. The hypocrites' saying (49:8-10) is framed «يقولونه احتقارا لهم». Light for «ومن يتوكل على الله». Al-Muyassar's «توبة نصوحًا» (Quran wording) not used. STAGING v4: Kept ambient (owner rule, Staging v4; picture review): c1 (48) is the Shaytan's promise and his turning back when the two armies met at Badr (the Shaytan, the angels and the battle are never drawn); a geometric plate only for Allah's severe punishment (48:34, after the Shaytan's words). c2 (49) is the saying of the hypocrites and those with sickness in their hearts, which both tafsirs place at Badr itself (Al-Muyassar: as they see the few Muslims and their many enemy; As-Sa'di: when the believers went forward to fight), so it stays ambient too, under the same night sky with camera moves only: no hypocrites, believers, town or gesture drawn. A seal plate for trusting His promise on the general statement of reliance (49:12, Al-Muyassar's gloss) and a geometric plate on the Name for Mighty and Wise (49:16)."
